# WHAT EAS LEAVES OUT OF THE UPLOAD. Written in build 17.
#
# When this file exists EAS reads IT for the upload tarball rather than
# .gitignore, so it has to say everything .gitignore says that matters to a
# build, plus the one thing that makes this repo's builds managed rather than
# bare: the generated native projects. artifacts/bolo-mobile/ios exists on the
# Mac, untracked, because the simulator dev client is built from it (chat 11).
# If EAS ever sees it, the build goes bare-workflow and every expo plugin stops
# applying. Before this file, only .gitignore stood between the two, and only
# while ios/ stayed untracked.
#
# eas-cli runs from artifacts/bolo-mobile, never the repo root, and the upload
# is the git root, which is why this lives at the git root.

# Generated native projects
artifacts/bolo-mobile/ios/
artifacts/bolo-mobile/android/

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules
dist
.expo
.expo-shared
*.tsbuildinfo
artifacts/bolo-mobile/web-build/

# Secrets and signing material
.env*
!.env*.example
*.p8
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.jks
*.mobileprovision
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
api-*.json
gcp-*.json
play-*.json
*service-account*.json
*-key.json

# Bulk that no build reads
attached_assets/
artifacts/bolo-social-clips/
qa/
.agents/
.cache/
.local/
.DS_Store
